name issue_76_rtx_v2_handover
describe Wi-Fi to LTE handover, RTX history as libwebrtc's RtpPacketHistory (#76 group 2)
# libwebrtc stores a packet when the pacer sends it, keeps it max(3 RTT, 1 s), culls it when the peer
# acknowledges it, and answers a repeat request only once per RTT. Seeds 1-5, with `keyframe v2`:
# repair overhead 29-39% and residual loss 0% with `rtx v2`, against 59-68% and 0.4-2.8% with `rtx v1`;
# libwebrtc (CI compare-webrtc, wifi_to_lte_handover): repair overhead 34%.
# Target (#76 / parity): within the parity band of libwebrtc's repair overhead.
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=4000kbps delay=15ms jitter=5ms queue=200ms
at 15s down
at 16.5s up capacity=1200kbps delay=60ms jitter=15ms loss=1%
reverse at 0s delay=15ms
reverse at 15s down
reverse at 16.5s up delay=60ms
expect repair.overhead_pct < 45
# Issue #355 with #361 (program.md 0.2; accepted by the Owner on 2026-10-24 at < 0.75): was < 0.5. With the tracker and XR RTT, seed 1 gives up on packets
# and requests a keyframe (0.68 %, 1 request); seeds 2-10 have 0. libwebrtc requests keyframes here too (0.2 per seed
# on main's compare-webrtc). Longest freeze seeds 1-10 mean 2028 ms, libwebrtc 2036. libwebrtc's per-seed residual loss
# isn't in sm_compare's data.
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 0.75
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 6000
